      "item_body": "<p>[K/U] Use the chain rule, in Leibniz notation, to find dy/dx at the given value of x.</p>\n<p>a. y = 3u^2 - 5u + 2, u = x^2 - 1, x = 2: dy/dx = <span id=\"blank_43a3c878-ad7c-4007-8483-a80c17f53c66\"></span></p>\n<p>b. y = 2u^3 + 3u^2, u = x + x^(1/2), x = 1: dy/dx = <span id=\"blank_12df75a6-f347-41b6-ac49-08b943ed6ccd\"></span></p>\n<p>c. y = u(u^2 + 3)^3, u = (x + 3)^2, x = -2: dy/dx = <span id=\"blank_81e5a811-09aa-42c7-906b-a468e517478b\"></span></p>\n<p>d. y = u^3 - 5(u^3 - 7u)^2, u = sqrt(x), x = 4: dy/dx = <span id=\"blank_8c8cb04b-14f1-404e-b8d1-18aedf6ff1ca\"></span></p>",
